    <h1>Hi, I'm Andrei.</h1>
    <p>
      I'm studying Immersive Software Engineering at the University of Limerick.
      I enjoy turning an idea into working software, especially when the code
      connects something on a screen to something in the physical world.
    </p>
    <p>
      My projects have taken me from reading sensors and sending radio telemetry
      with Velsat to collecting training images and experimenting with computer
      vision in ExGlass. They have also taught me that a working demonstration
      and a reliable system are different milestones.
    </p>
    <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
    <p>
      I write about the software I worked on: how a system fits together, why I
      changed an approach, and what went wrong before something started working.
      Hardware appears where it helps explain the code; the focus is on
      implementation and learning.
    </p>
